cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "rater-agreement: chance-corrected agreement statistics for any raters, human or model"
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Ciesielski
    given-names: Joanna
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-2397-3660"
repository-code: "https://github.com/joanna-ciesielski/rater-agreement"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A small, auditable, numpy-only implementation of chance-corrected
  inter-rater and intra-rater agreement statistics: percent agreement,
  Cohen's kappa (unweighted and weighted), Fleiss' kappa, Krippendorff's
  alpha with missing-data handling, ICC(1,1)/(2,1)/(3,1), bootstrap
  confidence intervals, kappa-paradox diagnostics (prevalence index, bias
  index, PABAK), test-retest agreement, decision flip rates, and a
  repeats-per-item sample-size planner. Built for settings where the
  reported coefficient must be traceable to a reference: every statistic
  is validated against hand-computed or published values. Applies equally
  to human raters and multi-sampled LLM judges.
keywords:
  - inter-rater reliability
  - intra-rater reliability
  - chance-corrected agreement
  - Cohen's kappa
  - kappa paradox
  - Krippendorff's alpha
  - intraclass correlation
  - LLM-as-judge
  - evaluation
